# ── Chapter 5 fidelity pins: "Voiding" ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/05-voiding.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the cross-file reconciliation or the prose guards

# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE — three kinds, and only one is a verdict. A FALSE on a
# corpus name this KB never mentions is real but empty: nothing could have made
# it TRUE. A non-corpus name is not a FALSE at all — the run aborts, pins not
# trustworthy. And a well-formed query on an argument its relation never
# carries is a vacuous green that passes forever. Article 0a closed the
# ASSERTION side only — a widening fact now aborts the run instead of loading —
# but a QUERY on an unmentioned name still answers a clean FALSE, so kind one
# is untouched. Pin a FALSE only where the KB could have said TRUE, and say in
# the comment what would flip it.

:expect-pins 39

# "Bela was examined by Gia and by Hex, and their pens come from different
#  bodies." — the cross-body requirement, exercised by the shipped case. These
#  two must stay adjacent: the rule needs one of each, so a pin on either alone
#  would pass while the pair had quietly become same-body.
? permits(Review, Gia).
# => TRUE

? permits(Tribunal, Hex).
# => TRUE

# THE FOUR FACTS THAT ACTUALLY SATISFY THE RULE. The block above pins the two
# credentials and the block below pins the outcome; between them sat the
# examining and the recording, by both signers, unpinned. Delete any one of
# these and `false(Bela)` stops deriving — which makes them premises, not
# scenery.
? judge(Gia, Bela).
# => TRUE

? capture(Gia, Bela).
# => TRUE

? judge(Hex, Bela).
# => TRUE

? capture(Hex, Bela).
# => TRUE

? false(Bela).
# => TRUE

# "One person's finding does not void a person."
? capture(Koa, Esa).
# => TRUE

# ...and the chapter now says exactly what kind of person Koa is: no act of
# judging, no seat, no pen. The prose used to claim both and the record says
# neither — these two pins are what keeps that sentence honest. Chapter 2's
# no-standing exhibit and chapter 1's "documented something" rest on the same
# two facts, so if either of these ever flips, three chapters move, not one.
? judge(Koa, Esa).
# => FALSE

? permits(Review, Koa).
# => FALSE

? false(Esa).
# => FALSE

# "You may not judge your family." — and the guard turns on the judge
? parent(Dev, Esa).
# => TRUE

? judge(Dev, Esa).
# => TRUE

? false(Dev).
# => TRUE

# "You may not lie." — Mira untouched, Lupo voided
? deceive(Lupo, Mira).
# => TRUE

? false(Mira).
# => FALSE

? false(Lupo).
# => TRUE

# "Vex's signature does not count" — the epoch carry
? rotten(Vex).
# => TRUE

# Wren's pen is from the OTHER body, and that is what keeps the next pin
# honest. Vex is Review-seated and carried-void, Wren is Convocation-seated
# and clean, so the pair satisfies cross-body and fails ONLY on Vex's carry.
# Put Wren back on the Electorate and false(Tyr) stays FALSE for the wrong
# reason — verified: with Wren here, deleting rotten(Vex) flips it TRUE.
? permits(Tribunal, Wren).
# => TRUE

? false(Tyr).
# => FALSE

# ── FIXTURES. MUST BE LAST IN THE FILE, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC ─────────────
# Everything below writes ground facts, and a ground fact is resident from the
# line it appears on and is never retracted. Any pin added after this point
# measures a widened record. Put new queries ABOVE this block.
#
# THE NAMES ARE FRESH ON PURPOSE, with one deliberate exception. A new fact
# naming EXISTING people can complete Article 4's multi-sig by accident — four
# such facts were once measured to flip `false(Tyr)` and destroy this chapter's
# carried-void case. The exception is Lupo, who has to be someone the record
# already calls a liar, so `false(Tyr)` is re-queried at the end of this block
# as a guard rather than as decoration.

# ── The independence condition, which no pin anywhere exercised ──────────────
# The block above about Dev and Esa LOOKS like this and is not: that is Article
# 5, parenthood between examiner and examined. This is the multi-sig conjunct,
# parenthood between the two SIGNERS — a different rule with a different head.
#
# The control has to be CROSS-BODY or it proves nothing: a same-body pair fails
# on the credential conjuncts first, and the void would be blocked for a reason
# that has nothing to do with kinship. So both credentials are pinned TRUE in
# the same breath as the blocked void. That pairing is the whole test.
# T1 fixtures: a new seat is not a pen. Each synthetic signer below carries an
# independently witnessed positive-clear status into the current record.
authorized(Sirefa, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Sirefa, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Sirefa, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Sirefa, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Sirefa, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Scionfa, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Scionfa, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Scionfa, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Scionfa, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Scionfa, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Unrela, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Unrela, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Unrela, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Unrela, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Unrela, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Unrelb, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Unrelb, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Unrelb, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Unrelb, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Unrelb, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Ambi, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Ambi, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Ambi, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Ambi, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Ambi, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Lupo, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Lupo, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Lupo, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Lupo, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Lupo, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Partnr, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Partnr, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Partnr, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Partnr, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Partnr, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Mara, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Mara, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Mara, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Mara, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Mara, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Maro, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Maro, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Maro, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Maro, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Maro, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Una, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Una, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Una, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Una, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Una, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
authorized(Uno, ClearStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Uno, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Uno, Epoch_Previous, ClearScope).
carries(Chronicle, Uno, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Uno, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, ClearCarry).

choose(Electorate, Sirefa).
choose(Convocation, Scionfa).
parent(Sirefa, Scionfa).
judge(Sirefa, Targ).
capture(Sirefa, Targ).
judge(Scionfa, Targ).
capture(Scionfa, Targ).

? permits(Review, Sirefa).
# => TRUE

? permits(Tribunal, Scionfa).
# => TRUE

? false(Targ).
# => FALSE

# ...and the same shape between strangers voids. Without this the pin above is
# just a void that did not happen.
choose(Electorate, Unrela).
choose(Convocation, Unrelb).
judge(Unrela, Targo).
capture(Unrela, Targo).
judge(Unrelb, Targo).
capture(Unrelb, Targo).
authorized(Unrela, IndependentReviewer, Targo).
authorized(Unrelb, IndependentReviewer, Targo).

? false(Targo).
# => TRUE

# ── One person holding both pens ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# "Give somebody everything... It still fails." Ambi is seated by BOTH bodies,
# judged and recorded — every act the rule asks of either signer, done twice
# over by one person. The void does not derive, and with both credentials
# pinned TRUE beside the FALSE, the only conjunct left standing is that the two
# names must belong to two people. This is also the liveness proof for the
# distinctness test Article 4's header keeps "for the day one person holds both
# pens": the cast now contains that day. The closing exhibit at the end of this
# file proves distinctness is the ONLY bar left.
choose(Electorate, Ambi).
choose(Convocation, Ambi).
judge(Ambi, Solo).
capture(Ambi, Solo).
authorized(Ambi, IndependentReviewer, Solo).
authorized(Ambi, IndependentReviewer, Solo).

? permits(Review, Ambi).
# => TRUE

? permits(Tribunal, Ambi).
# => TRUE

? false(Solo).
# => FALSE

# ── A voided man holding the pen, in the same snapshot ───────────────────────
# Lupo's own credibility is already gone in the shipped cast — the review body
# examined his deceitful finding and voided him. Seat him anyway. Nothing
# objects: he is voided and credentialed at once, and he can co-sign a stranger
# into the same condition he is in.
#
# The obvious repair is REFUSED, which is why this is a disclosure and not a
# bug report. Barring a voided person from the pen is rejected outright, and so
# is gating the void on its own signers. The chapter says why.
choose(Electorate, Lupo).

? false(Lupo).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Lupo).
# => TRUE

choose(Convocation, Partnr).
judge(Lupo, Frisk).
capture(Lupo, Frisk).
judge(Partnr, Frisk).
capture(Partnr, Frisk).
authorized(Lupo, IndependentReviewer, Frisk).
authorized(Partnr, IndependentReviewer, Frisk).

? false(Frisk).
# => TRUE

# THE GUARD. Everything above added facts naming an existing person; if any of
# it reached the shipped cast, this is where it shows.
? false(Tyr).
# => FALSE

# ── What actually closes it, one round late ──────────────────────────────────
# A raw mark no longer closes the pen. The predecessor status, both exact
# observations, and both carry witnesses must agree before the mark has legal
# force in the current record.
authorized(Lupo, VoidStatus, Epoch_Previous).
observe(Chronicle, Lupo, Epoch_Previous, VoidScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Lupo, Epoch_Previous, VoidScope).
carries(Chronicle, Lupo, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, VoidCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Lupo, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, VoidCarry).
rotten(Lupo).

? permits(Review, Lupo).
# => FALSE

# ── [v0.9 2026-08-02] THE INTIMATE PAIR, NAMED AT LAST ───────────────────────
# The kinship ruling: married and sibling joined the independence check beside
# ~parent. Mara and Maro — seated by different bodies, married to each other,
# every act the void rule asks performed on Targ2 — and the void does not
# derive: the marriage is the only failing conjunct. Una and Uno are the
# control: same seats, same acts, no recorded closeness, and Targ3 is voided.
# The guard is dead in the shipped cast (no marriage or siblinghood is
# recorded) and this pair is its liveness proof. The negative control is
# Article 0a itself: against the pre-ruling constitution the married fact
# aborts the run as unadmitted vocabulary.
choose(Electorate, Mara).
choose(Convocation, Maro).
married(Mara, Maro).
judge(Mara, Targ2).
capture(Mara, Targ2).
judge(Maro, Targ2).
capture(Maro, Targ2).

? false(Targ2).
# => FALSE

choose(Electorate, Una).
choose(Convocation, Uno).
judge(Una, Targ3).
capture(Una, Targ3).
judge(Uno, Targ3).
capture(Uno, Targ3).
authorized(Una, IndependentReviewer, Targ3).
authorized(Uno, IndependentReviewer, Targ3).

? false(Targ3).
# => TRUE

# ── The carry, written dishonestly ───────────────────────────────────────────
# A raw mark is inert. Even two carry entries without a witnessed predecessor
# basis are reported as forgery rather than converted into legal voiding.
? false(Forga).
# => FALSE

rotten(Forga).
carries(Chronicle, Forga, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, VoidCarry).
carries(TemporalReview, Forga, Epoch_Current, Epoch_Previous, VoidCarry).

? err(Forga, CarryForgery).
# => TRUE

? false(Forga).
# => FALSE

# ── THE EXHIBIT: distinctness was the only bar. MUST BE LAST ─────────────────
# An accepted rule loads into the KB and stays, so nothing may be pinned after
# this point — the base below is widened, exactly like chapter 14's closing
# exhibit, which is this file's precedent and its allowlist rationale in
# verify.sh section 4d. The rule is the void rule minus the requirement that
# the two signers differ. It loads, and Solo — untouchable above with every
# other condition met — is voided by one man's two pens. That flip is the
# proof that nothing but distinctness was holding, which is the section
# headline executed: it takes two, and one name written twice is one name.
:accept
all $a: all $audited: permits(Review, $a) & permits(Tribunal, $a) & authorized($a, IndependentReviewer, $audited) & judge($a, $audited) & capture($a, $audited) & ~deceive($a, $audited) -> false($audited).

? false(Solo).
# => TRUE
